            "review_title": "Review at Banh Canh Cua",
            "review_text": "Bryon K\nOsoyoos, Canada99 contributions\n0\nAuthentic Local Restaurant\nJan 2017 • Solo\nThis one is a bit off the tourist track. It survives by selling to a local clientele which usually means good food. And it delivers on that. Really just a storefront street food stand, you will share long tables and sit on stools. But the banh canh cua is well done. A very tasty soup with crab, shrimp, nice tender and lean pork in a very tasty broth. You won't see large chunks of crab, but the broth has a good amount of crab flavour. This is one of the few Vietnamese soups that has a thickness to the broth, from the tapioca based banh canh (noodles).\nRead more\nWritten January 14, 2017",
